  "result": "Excellent! All 119 tests pass. Here's a summary of the VAT implementation:\n\n## VAT Support\n\n**1. Added VAT calculation** (`src/invoices.js`)\n- **`lineVat()` function**: Calculates VAT for each line\n  - Formula: VAT = (lineTotal - lineDiscount) \u00d7 (vatRate \u00f7 100)\n  - Rounded to nearest cent per line\n  - Returns 0 if vatRate is undefined\n- **Updated `invoiceTotals()`**: Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n  - `vat` is the sum of all line VATs\n  - `total = subtotal - discount + vat`\n\n**2. Updated invoice rendering** (`src/render.js`)\n- Added VAT line display just above the total\n- Format: `VAT: \u20acX.XX`\n\n**3. Comprehensive test coverage** (`test/invoices.test.js`)\n- Added 13 new VAT tests covering:\n  - VAT calculation at different rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n  - VAT on discounted amounts\n  - VAT rounding per line\n  - Single and multiple VAT rates in one invoice\n  - Edge cases (100% discount, no VAT)\n\n**4. Updated render tests** (`test/render.test.js`)\n- Updated 4 render tests to account for VAT line\n- All tests now verify correct VAT calculation and display\n\n**Key decision implemented**: VAT is calculated per line on the amount **after discount**, rounded per line, and the invoice VAT is the sum of rounded line VATs\u2014never calculated as a percentage of invoice total. This ensures precise, line-level accounting.",
